SUMMARY:What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Nov 26 thru Dec 2**\n.\nUpcoming **mu
 sic events** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\
 n(Updates on Thurs morning)\n.\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & mark
 et events may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar
 -of-events\n.\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonp
 l.libcal.com/\nTech classes\, adult programs\, interesting stuff.. 😉\n.
 \n**Thu\; November 26** @ 8:30 am - 10:30 am\nHendersonville’s 14th Annu
 al Turkey Trot 5k\n$28.00 – $38.00\nKick off your Thanksgiving with a fu
 n-filled dash through Hendersonville at the 14th annual Turkey Trot to **b
 enefit Hope Coalition!** Whether you are a seasoned runner\, casual stroll
 er\, or just in it for the costumes\, this event is open to all-ages!\nhtt
 ps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/hendersonvilles-14th-annual-turkey-tr
 ot-5k\n.\n**November 27** @ 7:30 pm - 10:00 pm\; $$$\nA Flat Rock Playhous
 e Christmas Show – 10th Anniversary Special\nCelebrate ten dazzling year
 s of holiday cheer at Flat Rock Playhouse!\nFor a decade\, A Flat Rock Pla
 yhouse Christmas has been the cherished gathering that brings our communit
 y together\, where Broadway sparkle meets small-town heart and the spirit 
 of the season takes center stage.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event
 /a-flat-rock-playhouse-christmas-show-10th-anniversary-special/2026-11-27\
 nhttps://www.flatrockplayhouse.org/\n.\n**November 28**\nSmall Business Sa
 turday\nPlan your Christmas shopping downtown. A gift from a local busines
 s is a gift made or sold with love. Support our downtown businesses on Sma
 ll Business Saturday and all holiday season\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc
 .org/event/small-business-Saturday\nhttps://www.hendersonvillenc.gov/event
 s/holiday-cheer-downtown-hendersonville\n.\n**November 28** @ 8:00 am - 2:
 00 pm\; Free\nHenderson County Curb Market Christmas Open House\nThe Hende
 rson County Curb Market celebrates the holiday with a Christmas Open House
 . Visitors will enjoy a drop-in appearance from Santa and his elf\, compli
 mentary cookies\, hot cider and hot chocolate\, a raffle basket\, a childr
 en’s activity table\, a local authors signing\, a Native American story 
 teller and the community Peppermint Bear scavenger hunt. There is shopping
  for the perfect hand crafted gifts created by local vendors\, greenery\, 
 holiday decorations\, seasonal produce\, fresh baked goods\, honey\, prese
 rve and relishes.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/henderson-count
 y-curb-market-christmas-open-house\n.\n**Sunday\, November 29**\nSundayFun
 day with Peggy Ratusz & Friends\n4-6pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 82
 2 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n.\n**Thur\, December 3**\; 2:00pm - 4:00pm\n
 Movie Matinee- The Breadwinner\nHenderson Co Main library\nhttps://henders
 onpl.libcal.com/event/14834312\n.\n**December 4** @ 9:00 am - 4:00 pm\nBul
 lington Gardens Holiday Market\nJoin the Bullington Elves for our Annual H
 oliday Market. Shop for holiday greenery including custom and unique wreat
 hs\, crafts & gifts. Pre-order Fraser Fir trees\, Bullington calendars & A
 maryllis online!\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/bullington-garde
 ns-holiday-market/2026-12-04\nhttps://www.bullingtongardens.org/\n.\n**Dec
 ember 4** @ 5:00 pm - 8:00 pm\nOlde Fashioned Christmas\nan olde fashioned
  open house with all downtown Hendersonville’s wonderful assortment of d
 estination shops\, family friendly entertainment and fabulous eateries!\nH
 ear delightful Christmas stories told by Mrs. Hollyberry or take your pict
 ure with the Winter Prince and Princess. Stop and watch a master Ice Sculp
 tor at work and much more!\nHenderson County Parks and Recreation will acc
 ompany the event with Santa on the Square. It will include selfies with Sa
 nta\, hot cocoa\, games\, crafts\, specials guests and more. Santa on the 
 Square will be hosted in front of the Historic Courthouse in Downtown Hend
 ersonville.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/odle-fashioned-christ
 mas\n.\n**December 4** @ 6:30 pm - 7:30 pm\; $10\nSleepy Seahorse Shadow P
 uppet show\nStudio 116 is excited to announce new shows from the Sleepy Se
 ahorse Shadow Puppet Co. premiering Friday and Saturday Dec. 4 and 5. Each
  night will feature two productions: the African folktale ‘The Mantis an
 d the Moon’ and the new original story ‘Zephyr the Hare Sets Sail.’\
 nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/all-new-sleepy-seahorse-shadow-pu
 ppet-co-shows/2026-12-04\n.\n**December 5** @ 9:00 am - 1:00 pm\nChristmas
  Holiday Market at the Hendersonville Farmers Market\nEmbrace the holiday 
 spirit at our Christmas Holiday Market on Dec. 5\, from 9am-1pm at the his
 toric Train Depot! It’s your opportunity to find unique Christmas gifts\
 , festive decorations\, and delectable treats to elevate your holiday cele
 brations. Join us with over 30 merry vendors for a magical shopping experi
 ence!\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/christmas-holiday-market-at
 -the-hendersonville-farmers-market\n.\n**December 5** @ 5:00 pm - 7:00 pm\
 nHafla for Hope Bellydance Fundraiser\n“In Arabic \, the word Hafla simp
 ly means “party or gathering”. In our world\, it is a traditional comm
 unity celebration where dancers of all levels come together to perform in 
 a supportive environment. It isn’t about perfection\, it’s about conne
 ction\, community\, and the joy of dance” .\nThis fundraiser will be sup
 porting Safelight and Woman Helping Woman\, All proceeds go to Charity.\nT
 his event will be free admission\, and there will be a silent auction and 
 a special drink menu /mocktails to support our fundraiser\, So please join
  us for BellyDance with a cause\nGuidon Brewing Co.\; 415 8th Ave E.\nhttp
 s://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/hafla-for-hope-bellydance-fundraiser\n
 .\nThese are NOT hosted events and are posted for informational purposes o
 nly. Please make personal arrangements to meetup with friends and family.\
 nIf you wish to attend and host one of these events\, I will post the even
 t as an individual happening. Hosting only requires being focal point for 
 others and making introductions. Simple!!
