SUMMARY:Exercise Tr Pisgah Forest\; a Saunter
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A Walk in the Park\;**\nWe will Tour de P
 arks of the area. One at a time.\n**This Week: *Exercise Tr & Andy Cove:**
 *\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes hosted by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend
  to have pleasant surprises.\nRoute: Andy Cove Tr to English Chapel to Art
  Loeb Trhd & Back to Ranger Station.\n**Difficulty:** Moderate\; Mostly fl
 at earthen trail. Moderate climb is in the beginning..\n**Due to recent ev
 ents\, Ouija boards are no longer permitted.**\n**A Sloth Walking Team eve
 nt: A casual pace**\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4**\n**Up
  to 12 ppl are welcome to join us.**\nHike Distance: 2.25mi RT\; Accum asc
 ent: 200 ft\; Pace: **1.5mph**\nReturn Not earlier than: 11:15 am **(=1.75
  hrs)**\nWeather Check: Brevard\, NC\n**OPTIONAL:** Late lunch after the h
 ike.\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is NOT for those who 
 are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Dogs (and Masters) *
 *required** to be ‘on-leash'...\nIncessant prattlers will be assumed to 
 be having an affair.\nAll hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible 
 for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer of this
  event is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the or
 ganizer is only to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent i
 n any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this ev
 ent\, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\,
  its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illne
 ss\, or personal loss which might occur while participating in this activi
 ty or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant 
 further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, t
 o follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally s
 eparated from the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any ima
 ges collected on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngo
 rdie's contact: curmudgeonhiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.3
 93.0297 (talk & text)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05
 /albums**
